WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.608
A paper menu dies the day a price changes.

2
00:00:04.408 --> 00:00:08.333
Menu QR puts the whole menu behind one code per table.

3
00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:13.156
Diners scan, the kitchen sees the order, and nobody installs anything.

4
00:00:13.956 --> 00:00:18.308
Scan table four at Café Green and the menu opens in the browser.

5
00:00:18.758 --> 00:00:22.086
Switch to Arabic and the whole page flips right to left.

6
00:00:22.536 --> 00:00:26.120
Pick a cappuccino, choose the milk, and send it to the kitchen.

7
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.047
Seconds later it's a ticket on the board, under the right table.

8
00:00:30.847 --> 00:00:33.898
The hard part: one codebase serves every venue.

9
00:00:34.348 --> 00:00:38.103
Each table's code names the venue and the table, and it's signed.

10
00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:42.478
The server verifies that signature before it touches the database.

11
00:00:42.928 --> 00:00:47.045
Then the storefront renders in the venue's own design, one of twenty-eight.

12
00:00:47.495 --> 00:00:51.058
And the kitchen board polls for new tickets every three seconds.

13
00:00:51.858 --> 00:00:54.205
Full write-up at benarfa.com.

